  "raw_input": "When did the first bank come into existence that is part of an organization that serves rural areas of India with basic banking and financial services?",
  "ground_truth": "on 20 July 2009",
  "final_output": "The first bank in India that was established to serve rural areas with basic banking and financial services was the **Punjab National Bank (Punjab National Bank)**, but more specifically, the **Regional Rural Banks (RRBs)** were established to serve rural areas.\n\nHowever, the **first institution** specifically created to serve rural areas was the **Punjab, Sind, Sindh, and Gujarat (PSSG) Rural Bank**, which was established in **1969** as part of the Government of India's initiative to provide banking services to rural and underserved areas.\n\nBut the **first bank** established under the **Regional Rural Banks (RRBs)** scheme was the **Punjab Agricultural Credit and Rural Development Bank (PACRDB)**, which later became part of the RRB system.\n\nActually, the **first Regional Rural Bank** was established in **1970** — the **Punjab National Bank (PNB) Regional Rural Bank** — in **1970**.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\n**1970**\n\nThis is when the first Regional Rural Bank (RRB) was established in India to serve rural areas with basic banking and financial services.",
